    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "True or False? Let $A$ and $B$ be sets in a universal set $U$.\n\n$A\\cap\\overline B=A\\cap\\overline{(A\\cap B)}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "True.",
      "worked": "True. Among elements of $A$, the elements belonging to $A\\cap B$ are exactly those in $B$. Excluding them leaves the elements of $A$ outside $B$ on both sides.",
